{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"86372cbd4b76439edb9041576abb7dfc01d63bf176d0f30946645635dc750c60","digest":{"component_or_area":"bridge suggest-mapping command","key_entities":["rebar bridge suggest-mapping","mapping_probe.py","mapping_config.py","bridge.py","_bridge_commands.py","_config_writer._emit_nested_toml","_config_writer._emit_config_toml","jira.JIRA.issue_types","jira.JIRA.priorities","jira.JIRA.issue_link_types","jira.JIRA.statuses","jira.JIRA.createmeta_issuetypes","jira.JIRA.transitions","rebar.toml","[tool.rebar.mapping]","issue_types","statuses","link_types","priority_map","hierarchy","status_map","create_defaults","projects.<KEY>"],"problem_keywords":["mapping config","jira probe","vocabulary discovery","axis seeding","toml emission","read-only command"],"propositions":["A new READ-ONLY `rebar bridge suggest-mapping <PROJECT>` command probes a live Jira project via pycontribs and emits a suggested `[tool.rebar.mapping]` block seeded with discovered vocabulary and identity-seed axis maps.","The probe discovers issue types, statuses, link types, priorities, and hierarchy from public JIRA methods; per-project status lists are unavailable so global statuses are used with documented limitation.","With `--write`, the command deep-merges discovered mapping under an existing or new `rebar.toml` while preserving flat `[jira]` and `[tracker]` siblings; existing hand-edited keys are never overwritten.","Transition hints are collected via search+transitions on sample issues per type and flagged as best-effort/partial since Jira returns only current-status transitions.","Create-defaults stubs are emitted only for required createmeta fields absent from the baseline outbound-create path.","Nested TOML serialization uses a new orchestrator `_emit_config_toml` that delegates flat items to `_emit_toml` and nested `[mapping.*]` to `_emit_nested_toml`, preserving the fail-closed contract on `_emit_toml`."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787554598386357001,"uuid":"92d422a2-2779-4078-a510-dce40c90deec"}